# Real bug found 2026-09-25: stale, months-old __pycache__/*.pyc files
# (gitignored, but Docker's COPY doesn't honor .gitignore -- only
# .dockerignore) were getting baked into the dashboard image on every
# build. Python's import system doesn't always recompile a .pyc against a
# freshly-COPYed .py source if their mtimes end up in an order that looks
# up-to-date, so a real code fix (macro_risk_analyzer.py's
# SECTOR_SENSITIVITY_MAP backtest correction) silently kept running the
# OLD compiled bytecode after a full rebuild -- found by directly
# comparing the running container's live output against a fresh direct
# script run of the same code, which disagreed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

.git/
.venv/
venv/
*.log
